    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access — Trusted Relationship", "technique": "T1199", "what_happened": "At 2026-03-20 10:30:14 CEST (a weekday mid-morning, OUTSIDE any documented MSP maintenance window), the MSP service account msp.svc authenticated to the RMM management portal on 10.108.57.10. The authentication originated from data.srcip=185.220.101.47 — an IP NOT on the MSP's documented source-IP allowlist. The MSP relationship normally restricts msp.svc to scheduled maintenance windows from a known static MSP egress IP; this login matches neither constraint. Wazuh rule 5715 'Auth from unrecognized MSP IP' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1199.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 5715 fired on data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=msp.svc with data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=185.220.101.47 — a source IP outside the MSP allowlist. The univariate signature: trusted service account + auth event + source IP not in the partner allowlist + timestamp outside maintenance window.", "first_seen": "2026-03-20T10:30:14+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Execution / Lateral Movement — RMM Remote Command", "technique": "T1199", "what_happened": "Between 10:32:31 and 10:33:34 CEST, the same msp.svc session issued RMM-style remote commands (POST /api/v1/remote/command, cmd=whoami) against FOUR distinct managed endpoints in rapid succession: 10.108.57.177, 10.108.57.184, 10.108.57.198, 10.108.57.211 — one every ~21 seconds. A legitimate MSP maintenance job targets a named change-ticket host set; issuing whoami to four endpoints in 63 seconds with no associated change ticket is reconnaissance of the managed fleet, not maintenance. Wazuh rule 92900 'MSP account accessing multiple endpoints simultaneously' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1199.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92900 fired when data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=msp.svc generated remote-command rule.description events against >2 distinct data.dstip values within a 60-second window. The signature: single MSP principal + remote-command rule + >=3 distinct managed-endpoint destinations + sub-minute span.", "first_seen": "2026-03-20T10:32:31+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Discovery — Managed Client Enumeration", "technique": "T1199", "what_happened": "At 10:40:02 CEST the msp.svc session issued GET /api/v1/clients/list against the RMM portal — a full enumeration of every managed client endpoint. This call returns the complete inventory of the MSP's managed fleet (the attacker's blast radius). The clients/list endpoint is normally invoked only by the MSP's automated scheduler principal during nightly sync, NOT interactively by msp.svc mid-morning. This is blast-radius reconnaissance: the actor is mapping every reachable managed endpoint before deciding where to pivot. Wazuh flagged the call as anomalous for the msp.svc principal.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlated a clients/list enumeration rule.description event with data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=msp.svc and data.srcip=185.220.101.47 — the same off-allowlist IP from step 1. The enumeration call issued by the interactive msp.svc principal (not the scheduler principal) within the same anomalous session closes the chain: off-window login → fleet recon → full inventory enumeration.", "first_seen": "2026-03-20T10:40:02+0200"}
